often when people think about leading  change or implementing change in  organizations they always think at the  30,000 feet they're very abstract we  usually talk about generalities such as  how do I communicate how do I engage how  do I reach out to people but often this  30,000 feet orientation simply means  that we're fighting the campaign of  leading change and implementing change  as a mayor by contrast if you really  want to succeed in embedding change  within organizations thinking about it  just as an air war is not enough you  really have to think about it as a  ground war and in order to fight that  ground war which is going to be messy  which is going to be surprised Laden  you've actually got to have not only a  plan that gives you confidence but a  plan that emphasizes flexibility press  is an acronym it consists of five  letters each letter denotes if you will  a sub process of implementing change  remember it's a sub process and not a  stage that means you have to think of  these five sub processes in tandem what  does press stand for the first sub  process is persuading persuading has to  do with how do you influence the  emotions of people so that you can  change their beliefs in the hope that  they will actually you know generate new  behaviors that are much more relevant to  the organization they are in the press  framework stands for recruiting support  and overcoming resistance any worthwhile  change will face opposition of course  individuals oppose change for a variety  of reasons but if we understand the  target markets behind change we can  understand those individual reasons and  here were much more concerned with how  groups of people can stymie and block  change so we're interested if you will  in the network structure of resistance  and how to break off  when that resistance in organizations  the third element of the press framework  is II and is very important it's  actually about energizing new behavior a  very powerful way in which we can change  the beliefs of people is getting them to  do things and energizing is all about  getting people to do things given how  you supply them information given how  you cleverly design rewards or empower  individuals the other sub process in the  press framework is staffing staffing  actually has to do with how do you put  together a change team and here who  should be on the change team what does  that actually convey in terms of  credibility of the change initiative and  so forth and we'll talk about how the  change team may actually be related to  the executive committee or the executive  leadership of the enterprise and how  various teams can bud off from the  change team to implement subtasks that  are part of the overall change the final  s of course is sequencing sequencing has  to do with the ordering of the actions  and these actions may have to do with  persuading or energizing or recruiting  or staffing figuring out when to do what  is important so what we'll actually  focus on in the sequencing module is  what do we need to do before day one of  the change what do we need to do on day  one what do we need to do by day ten day  20 we'll also build an opportunity for  review and if you have a plan like that  the chief consequences confidence but it  will also give you again opportunity for  review and editing and then you can  actually see how much of persuasion do  you want to emphasize how much of  energizing do you want to emphasize and  what is it you want to do to ensure that  as you're implementing the change there  is momentum rather than fatigue there is  excitement rather than cynicism
 

